    "body": "I have this in my `server.py` ...\r\n\r\n```\r\nif __name__ == '__main__':\r\n    if 'serve' in sys.argv:\r\n        uvicorn.run(app=app, host='0.0.0.0', port=5000, log_level=\"info\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n... which I've learned cannot be used to enable auto-reloading.  For that, I'm told I have to actually run uvicorn from the terminal as such:\r\n\r\n```\r\nuvicorn example:app --debug (or I think its --reload now)\r\n```\r\n\r\nAnyhow, is there any way I can do the auto-reload when the application is running in a docker container. I've played with the `Dockerfile` and my `docker-compose.yml` file to see if I can make this work but so far I've been unsuccessful.",
